# B.8.3 Main Models: Englishness (Continuous) {#sec-b8-engl}

The Englishness cultural DV models replicate the Britishness structure with Englishness as the identity moderator, following the same logic as Appendix B.3.

## B.8.3.1 Local Unemployment Rate {#sec-b8-engl-unemp}

Baseline specifications show no significant unconditional unemployment effect. The interaction models reveal a negative Englishness main effect (β ≈ −0.017, p \< 0.05), a positive and significant unemployment main effect (β ≈ 0.020, p \< 0.05), and a negative and significant interaction term (β ≈ −0.003, p \< 0.05), robust to age controls. This mirrors the directional structure observed in the Britishness unemployment models, though attenuated in magnitude, and indicates that higher local unemployment is associated with more permissive cultural attitudes at higher Englishness levels, with the association weakening as Englishness decreases.

```{r b8-engl-unemp-main}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Unemp only"    = m_u0.1_eng,
    "(2) + Englishness" = m_u1_eng,
    "(3) Unemp + Age"   = m_u0.2_eng,
    "(4) + Englishness" = m_u2_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", unemployment_rate = "Unemp. rate (local)", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.13. Local Unemployment Rate and Cultural Immigration Attitudes: Main Effects (Englishness)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigCultural.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

```{r b8-engl-unemp-int}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Interaction"       = m_u3_eng,
    "(2) Interaction + Age" = m_u4_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", unemployment_rate = "Unemp. rate (local)",
                  "engl:unemployment_rate" = "Englishness × Unemp. rate", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.14. Local Unemployment Rate × Englishness: Interaction Models (Cultural DV)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigCultural.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

## B.8.3.2 Claimant Count {#sec-b8-engl-claimant}

Main-effect specifications show no significant unconditional claimant association. The interaction models yield a negative and significant Englishness main effect (β ≈ −0.037, p \< 0.001), a non-significant claimant main effect, and a positive and marginally significant interaction term (β ≈ 0.003, p \< 0.05), consistent across both specifications. This directional pattern parallels the Britishness claimant result, though the interaction is smaller in magnitude, and indicates that the conditional structure for claimant count extends to Englishness as an identity moderator.

```{r b8-engl-claimant-main}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Claimant only"  = m_c0.1_eng,
    "(2) + Englishness"  = m_c1_eng,
    "(3) Claimant + Age" = m_c0.2_eng,
    "(4) + Englishness"  = m_c2_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", claimant_rate = "Claimant count (local)", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.15. Claimant Count and Cultural Immigration Attitudes: Main Effects (Englishness)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigCultural.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

```{r b8-engl-claimant-int}
modelsummary(
  list(
    "(1) Interaction"       = m_c3_eng,
    "(2) Interaction + Age" = m_c4_eng
  ),
  coef_rename = c(engl = "Englishness", claimant_rate = "Claimant count (local)",
                  "engl:claimant_rate" = "Englishness × Claimant count", age = "Age"),
  gof_map = GOF_MAP,
  stars   = c("*" = .05, "**" = .01, "***" = .001),
  title   = "Table B8.16. Claimant Count × Englishness: Interaction Models (Cultural DV)",
  notes   = "Individual and wave FE. SEs clustered by respondent. DV: immigCultural.",
  escape  = FALSE,
  output  = "kableExtra"
) |> kable_styling()
```

## B.8.3.3 Local Income (ASHE) {#sec-b8-engl-income}

Local income shows no significant main effect in any specification, and the Englishness × local income interaction term is non-significant in both models. Unlike the immigSelf Englishness income result in Appendix B.3, there is no evidence here that local earnings condition cultural immigration attitudes through Englishness. The income null is therefore consistent across both identity moderators for the cultural DV.

```{r b8-engl-income-main}
